<title>JORDAN: Jordan Aug foreign reserves rise 1.7 pct vs July.</title>
<headline>Jordan Aug foreign reserves rise 1.7 pct vs July.</headline>
<dateline>AMMAN 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Central Bank of Jordan's total foreign reserves rose 1.7 percent in August from the previous month, the bank said in its latest monthly bulletin.</p>
<p>			 (All figures in millions of dinars)</p>
<p>				  Aug 96  July 96	1995   1994</p>
<p>    Total foreign assets  2,308   2,269	  2,185  1,904</p>
<p>  * Foreign assets	  877.7   868.9	  647.5  578.7</p>
<p> ** Foreign exchange	1,290   1,258	  1,397  1,186</p>
<p>    Gold			139.7   139.5	  138.9  139.1</p>
<p>NOTE -- (*)includes foreign loans and grants.</p>
<p>(**) includes a 35 percent compulsory reserve requirement imposed on foreign currency deposits held by Jordanian banks.</p>
<p>The bank's figures do not provide a breakdown that shows the country's key net foreign currency cash reserves, currently around two-month imports levels and close to the IMF target of $620 million for 1996.</p>
<p>$1=0.7080 dinar</p>
<p>- Amman newsroom, 962 6 623 776</p>
